</section>

<!-- MARQUEE -->
<div class="marquee"><div class="track">
  <div class="seg"><b>Valve-Cover Gaskets</b><b>Oil-Pan Gaskets</b><b>Filter-Housing Seals</b><b>Rear Main Seals</b><b>Leak Diagnosis</b></div>
  <div class="seg"><b>Valve-Cover Gaskets</b><b>Oil-Pan Gaskets</b><b>Filter-Housing Seals</b><b>Rear Main Seals</b><b>Leak Diagnosis</b></div>
</div></div>

<!-- STAT BAND -->
<section class="stats"><div class="container">
  <div class="statc"><b>#1</b><span>German Repair We See</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>4</b><span>German Marques</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>OEM</b><span>Gaskets &amp; Seals</span></div>
  <div class="statc"><b>2010</b><span>Independent Since</span></div>
</div></section>

<!-- INTRO -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Oil leak repair, done right</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Find the leak. Fix it once.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose reveal">
      <p>Searching for <span class="kw">oil leak repair near me</span> in San&nbsp;Antonio? Oil leaks are the single most common thing we see on German cars — and almost always a failed gasket or seal, not the engine itself. As the rubber and cork in <span class="kw">valve-cover gaskets</span>, oil-pan gaskets and filter-housing seals ages and bakes in Texas heat, it shrinks and cracks, and oil starts to weep. Left alone, it drips onto hot exhaust (that burning smell), fouls sensors, and slowly runs you low.</p>
      <p>At <span class="kw">German Car Specialists</span>, we don't throw parts at it. We clean the area, run the engine, and trace the leak to its true origin — because oil travels, and the wet spot is rarely the source. Then we replace the failed gasket or seal with OEM-quality parts and back it with our 24-month / 24,000-mile warranty. Whether it's a quick valve-cover job or a deeper oil-pan or rear-main-seal repair, you get an honest, upfront <span class="kw">oil pan leak repair cost</span> before we start.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SERVICES -->
<section class="sec alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we do</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Every oil leak, traced &amp; sealed.</h2>
      <p class="lead">From a weeping valve cover to a rear main seal — the full range of German oil-leak repair.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="svc-grid">
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="search"></i></div><h3>Oil Leak Diagnosis</h3><p>Degrease, run and trace with UV dye to find the real source — not the wet spot.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="layers"></i></div><h3>Valve-Cover Gasket</h3><p>The most common German oil leak — gasket and grommets renewed to spec.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="container"></i></div><h3>Oil-Pan Gasket</h3><p>Pan reseal with the correct OEM gasket and torque sequence, done right the first time.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="filter"></i></div><h3>Oil Filter Housing Gasket</h3><p>A classic BMW &amp; Audi leak that drips onto the belt and exhaust — sealed properly.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="circle-dot"></i></div><h3>Rear Main &amp; Cam Seals</h3><p>Deeper crankshaft and camshaft seal leaks handled by techs who do them often.</p></div>
      <div class="svc reveal"><div class="ico"><i data-lucide="gauge"></i></div><h3>Turbo &amp; Oil-Line Seals</h3><p>Turbo feed/return lines and fittings that seep under boost — inspected and resealed.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BMW HOOK -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="n54 reveal">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">BMW Oil Leaks</span>
        <h2>The BMW oil leaks we fix every week.</h2>
        <p>If you own a BMW, an oil leak isn't a question of if — it's when. The valve-cover gasket and the oil filter housing gasket are near-universal leaks as these engines age, and they drip straight onto the belt and exhaust. We've sealed enough of them to do it efficiently and correctly.</p>
        <p>For BMW-specific work and known failure points, see our <a class="inline" href="/bmw-repair-san-antonio">BMW repair page</a> — or just book below and we'll trace it.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="fail">
        <li><i data-lucide="layers"></i><span><b>Valve-cover gasket</b> — cracks with heat and weeps down the block</span></li>
        <li><i data-lucide="filter"></i><span><b>Oil filter housing gasket</b> — leaks onto the belt; a classic N-series job</span></li>
        <li><i data-lucide="container"></i><span><b>Oil-pan gasket</b> — seeps with age; resealed to factory torque</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BY MAKE -->
