        <div class="who"><span class="av">RB</span><div><b>Rafael B.</b><span>Audi S4</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="rcard reveal">
        <div class="rs" data-stars></div>
        <p>"Oil-pan gasket on my Mercedes was seeping. Fair quote, done next day, no surprises. They treat the car like it's their own."</p>
        <div class="who"><span class="av">SP</span><div><b>Sandra P.</b><span>Mercedes E350</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Oil Leak FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq reveal">
      <details><summary>How much does oil leak repair cost?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">It depends entirely on the source. A valve-cover gasket is a relatively quick job; an oil-pan gasket or rear main seal takes more labor. Independent repair runs well below dealer pricing for the same OEM parts, and we always diagnose and quote before any work so there are no surprises.</div></details>
      <details><summary>What does an oil pan leak repair cost?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">An oil-pan gasket reseal is more involved than a valve cover because the pan often sits behind a subframe or covers. We give an exact, upfront oil pan leak repair cost after confirming it's actually the pan — oil travels, so we verify the source first rather than assuming.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Is it safe to drive with an oil leak?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">A small weep can be monitored briefly, but don't ignore it. Oil dripping on a hot exhaust is a fire and smoke risk, leaks tend to worsen, and running low on oil can damage the engine. If you're seeing spots or low-oil warnings, get it diagnosed soon.</div></details>
      <details><summary>What are the signs of a valve cover gasket leak?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">A burning-oil smell after driving, oil pooling in the spark-plug valley, smoke from the engine bay, and oil residue down the side of the engine. It's the most common German oil leak and usually a straightforward fix when caught early.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Can you find a leak if you're not sure where it's coming from?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">Yes — that's the point of a proper diagnosis. We degrease the engine, add UV dye, run it, and pinpoint the true origin with a black light. Oil migrates, so guessing wastes your money; tracing finds it.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Do you repair oil leaks on all German makes?<span class="pl"></span></summary><div class="fa">Yes — BMW, Audi, VW, Mercedes-Benz and Porsche. Gasket and seal leaks are universal across German engines, and we stock OEM parts and know each platform's signature leak points.</div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

